\"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"adebbe3e897ad3735c4158dfa54fe1471ef1e1e4e72c7b2d8920006f4160ec70","event_uuid":"0f5d5f21-4c70-4679-981e-67578eccce99","position":{"commit_sha":"253c0a3e266aa380960a3309e8dd2857702cc7c5","position":"1793835064156204907-0f5d5f21-4c70-4679-981e-67578eccce99"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"0a62b7889e80990d80d072e70f413449bb53671367212b5168361d3a8ca23449","event_uuid":"d8fd454b-1051-40c4-8943-a504359fec1c","position":{"commit_sha":"24c6a0fd5c4640d9dbc451d3c5ed324ca6601edd","position":"1793845850380499490-d8fd454b-1051-40c4-8943-a504359fec1c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"e3d429e8d9a23f7ff4011a589324737129e7ed584811fb935fb4dad60344f6a7","event_uuid":"f41b2ee9-3205-45d2-88a1-07c7f1100180","position":{"commit_sha":"006b2a2294d028c6e2b2c8622459847a965c54c0","position":"1793846052568660381-f41b2ee9-3205-45d2-88a1-07c7f1100180"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Released back to `open`; the claim is withdrawn.\n\nThis ticket was claimed on a mistaken read that it carried the\n`complexity-reduction` tag. It does not — it is eval CI infrastructure\n(the `prompt-eval.yml` live arm calls `ev.run_eval` with no gate session,\nso every case errors, `run_eval` records them as unscored rather than as a\ncrash, and `continue-on-error: true` downgrades the result to an advisory\nwarning). Real defect, correctly specified, but not complexity reduction.\n\nPlan review PASSED and was certified at\n`4c4e9b2f0ba89663c9d6ac86c7297690288d6106` (job\n1793822616425741639-2dd194319b2f4ccbb56fc89773b2692b), so whoever picks this\nup next can check currency with `rebar review-plan <id> --status` instead of\npaying for a fresh review. No code was written and no worktree was created.","timestamp":1793823897679082113},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Removed the `complexity-reduction` tag. This stays an open, valid bug — the live prompt-eval\nCI job really does score 0.0 on every spec — but it is not part of the complexity-reduction\nprogram, so it should not count against that program's census.\n\nTwo independent reasons, both from the operator's stated scope for that program:\n\n1. Evals are out of scope for complexity remediation. Running an eval does not reduce\n   complexity.\n2. The program's working test is whether the change DELETES something. Fixing a `run_eval`\n   call site that sits outside a gate session is a repair, not a deletion.\n\nTags remaining: `evals`, `ci`. Priority 1 is unchanged and the ticket is untouched otherwise.\n","timestamp":1793826378208996670}],"created_at":1793760466971365145,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"a993ab40-98ce-4da7-9ccb-631cdead131d","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"e508-ce6c-2e52-4adc"}],"description":"# Live prompt-eval CI job scores coverage 0.0 on every spec\n\n## The gap\n\n`.github/workflows/prompt-eval.yml`'s `eval-live` job calls `ev.run_eval(pid, max_cases=cap)`\ndirectly (`:136`). It does **not** wrap the call in `rebar.llm.gate_source.gate_read_root`, and\nit does **not** set `REBAR_GATE_ALLOW_UNGATED`.\n\nSince epic raze-vet-ditch landed the agent-op safeguard, every agentic filesystem tool call\nmade outside a gate session raises:\n\n> agentic filesystem tools was attempted OUTSIDE the repo-snapshot gate process (epic\n> raze-vet-ditch): a tool-using agent must run inside rebar.llm.gate_source.gate_read_root\n> (attested snapshot or explicit local), never against the server's mutable checkout.\n\n(`src/rebar/llm/gate_context.py:144-162`)\n\n`run_eval` treats a solver exception as an **UNSCORED case, not a crash**\n(`src/rebar/llm/evals/eval.py:670-682`), so the job does not fail loudly. It records every case\nas a run error, computes `coverage = 0.0`, fails `coverage_ok`, and reports\n`epoch_pass = [false, false, false]`.\n\nThe job is `continue-on-error: true` (`:95`) and only emits\n`::warning::live eval regressions (advisory)`. So a **total** scoring failure is\nindistinguishable from an ordinary advisory regression, and the live eval corpus has not\nactually been scoring anything since the safeguard landed.\n\n## Reproduction (measured)\n\nFull dataset, no cap, worktree `impl-e508` at `origin/main` 0e7401446c58:\n\n```\npython -c \"from rebar.llm.evals import eval as ev; ev.run_eval('code-review-tests')\"\n→ passed=false  coverage=0.0  epoch_pass=[false,false,false]  elapsed=40.4s\n```\n\nAll **117** case-runs (39 cases x 3 epochs) carry the identical gate error in the JUnit\n`message=` attribute. 40 seconds for 117 agentic code reviews is itself the tell: no model\ncall was ever made.\n\nWrapping the same call in a local-mode gate session makes the run proceed and reach the model:\n\n```python\nhandle = gate_source.resolve_gate_handle(None, gate_source.SOURCE_LOCAL, root, fetch=False)\nwith gate_source.gate_read_root(handle):\n    res = ev.run_eval(\"code-review-tests\", repo_root=root)\n```\n\n## Why it matters\n\nAny AC of the form \"the eval spec scores at or above its recorded pass bar, reproducible from\nthe committed spec\" is currently **not reproducible from the committed CI path** — only from a\nhand-wrapped local run. Several closed stories carry exactly that AC shape.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The `eval-live` job's live step runs `run_eval` inside a gate session, choosing the\n      source mode explicitly rather than relying on the configured default. `REBAR_GATE_ALLOW_UNGATED`\n      is NOT used — the override is an audited escape hatch, not the fix.\n- [ ] A regression test asserts that the eval entry point used by CI runs under a gate session:\n      with the safeguard active and no override set, the entry point completes with\n      `coverage > 0` against an injected offline `solve`, and the unwrapped call is shown to\n      produce run errors. The test must fail against the current workflow's call shape.\n- [ ] `run_eval` (or the CI entry point) distinguishes \"every case errored\" from \"cases scored\n      and failed\" — a 0.0-coverage epoch is reported as a RUN FAILURE, not an advisory\n      regression, so this class of total failure cannot be silent again.\n- [ ] The portability constraint holds: the gate-session requirement is enforced in-process,\n      not by a GitHub-Actions-only step, so a project on another CI provider or no CI provider\n      gets the same behaviour.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"d07f65ee-e8c5-492d-ab9b-80afc10ee8f3","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["evals","ci","complexity-reduction"],"ticket_id":"77b6-868f-f4bd-461f","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Live prompt-eval CI job scores coverage 0.0 on every spec — run_eval is called outside a gate session","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["faccd675-4bbf-48cf-8e6a-9641c1ac5d37","0821b4f0-eb3b-4816-afa4-6eae1947b130","d07f65ee-e8c5-492d-ab9b-80afc10ee8f3","0e805211-47db-491a-84c4-5d9af6f9acf9","ca00eb6a-ce1d-42a9-96a8-5688b9d7eb62","61cbd9c3-3da1-453b-bcdb-1337d98b66d4","4a39e484-e210-48f6-b160-400549bab094","f7604360-eaaa-4a37-8340-f1bf0d147773","00b28adc-ce3b-4d67-9e0c-3be17cabf146","0f5d5f21-4c70-4679-981e-67578eccce99","d8fd454b-1051-40c4-8943-a504359fec1c","f41b2ee9-3205-45d2-88a1-07c7f1100180"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793846052568660382,"uuid":"885ad87f-50fb-4aed-8cc6-0a19102f4858"}